  Can It Run a Full Company on Its Own?

  No — not even close. Here's why:

  This codebase is an infrastructure control plane for AI agents. It manages how agents are authorized, governed, and metered. It does not contain the actual business logic to run a company. What's missing entirely:

  - No marketing module — no campaign automation, SEO agents, email workflows, social scheduling
  - No sales module — no CRM, lead scoring, pipeline management, outreach agents
  - No finance module — no accounting, AP/AR, payroll, financial reporting
  - No HR module — no hiring workflows, onboarding, performance management
  - No customer support — no ticket routing, escalation, resolution agents
  - No product/engineering management — no sprint planning, bug triage, roadmap agents

  What you do have is the operating layer that would govern and orchestrate such agents if they were built and registered. Think of it as Kubernetes — it can't run your app until you deploy your containers.

